# Decision: invoice totals are computed on the server only

File name in a project: `docs/decisions/2026-03-12_invoice-totals-server.md`.
The five sections below are exactly the fields `tools/decisions-check.sh` requires.
No other `##` headings are allowed; each needs at least one line of content.
(This example is invented; the checker's field names are German.)

## Kontext
The web client and the mobile app both summed invoice lines themselves and rounded differently (per line vs. per total). Customers saw cent differences between screen and PDF.

## Entscheid
Totals, tax and rounding are computed once, on the server (`InvoiceService.totals`). Clients display the returned numbers and never calculate them.

## Verworfen
- Shared rounding library in both clients: still two call sites, drifts at the next update.
- Rounding on the client with a server check: the check would only report, not fix.

## Woran man den Fehler merkt
A support ticket "PDF and screen differ by 1 cent", or any `sum(`/`toFixed(` over invoice lines outside the server (the project's guard greps for it).

## Wie zurückdrehen
Revert the commit that removed client-side summing; the server field `totals` stays and is simply ignored by the clients. No data migration needed.
